<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Birmingham Strikes, 1992</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;In&amp;nbsp;the 1990s, Sierra Leone&amp;nbsp;suffered through a&amp;nbsp;brutal civil war that resulted in the deaths of tens of thousands of people.&amp;nbsp; The rebels, known as the Revolutionary United Front (RUF) were infamous because of the&amp;nbsp;atrocities they committed.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;The war was eventually brought to a close when the United Kingdom intervened in 2000.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This scenario presents a fictional mission that might have been undertaken by the United Kingdom against the RUF early in the conflict.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In the historical conflict, the RUF did capture a large number of weapons from Sierra Leone (and later from some of the UN peacekeepers dispatched to the area) and countries&amp;nbsp;such as&amp;nbsp;Libya also supplied the RUF with additional weapons.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;When designing the RUF&amp;nbsp;forces for this scenario, I relied mostly on available historical information, but&amp;nbsp;provided the rebels with a few additional Libyan&amp;nbsp;weapons to make them a bit more of a challenge.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;-------------------------------------------------------&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;A delta template .ini file has been included in the .zip file to assist in updating the scenario to any future versions of the database.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;Scenario Author: Mark Gellis&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
